[[:db/retract 17592186162652 :question/answer-fields 17592186161174] {:db/id 17592186162020 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9d231abd-db3d-5d11-9253-820e7eb51742"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162652 :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection matrix that maps $x\\in {R}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-4$ of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nMoreover, ${u}_{i}\\cdot {u}_{i}^{T}$ is the projection matrix corresponding to ${u}_{i}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to $\\lambda =-4.$ Computing $A-(-4)I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+4I & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}]+4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-2{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖v‖=\\sqrt{5}.$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we obtain the normalized eigenvector: \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, the required orthogonal projection matrix is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {u}^{T} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ebade115-5b0c-52d7-94cc-8ec9e5babad9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ebade115-5b0c-52d7-94cc-8ec9e5babad9" :answer-field/id #uuid "ebade115-5b0c-52d7-94cc-8ec9e5babad9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f93a6cf9-78b6-546d-ba88-361fc48a056a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e9f4f75f-447a-5e0c-a1d6-feae985a30a3" "answer-d6effcc8-e643-5b20-9090-b3855faacab9" "answer-f93a6cf9-78b6-546d-ba88-361fc48a056a" "answer-1556dc1b-0c8b-54e0-a340-18371f592ed3" "answer-286d06a8-1050-59ed-a665-558d840c2aae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9f4f75f-447a-5e0c-a1d6-feae985a30a3" :answer/id #uuid "e9f4f75f-447a-5e0c-a1d6-feae985a30a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6effcc8-e643-5b20-9090-b3855faacab9" :answer/id #uuid "d6effcc8-e643-5b20-9090-b3855faacab9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f93a6cf9-78b6-546d-ba88-361fc48a056a" :answer/id #uuid "f93a6cf9-78b6-546d-ba88-361fc48a056a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1556dc1b-0c8b-54e0-a340-18371f592ed3" :answer/id #uuid "1556dc1b-0c8b-54e0-a340-18371f592ed3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-286d06a8-1050-59ed-a665-558d840c2aae" :answer/id #uuid "286d06a8-1050-59ed-a665-558d840c2aae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d231abd-db3d-5d11-9253-820e7eb51742" :question/id #uuid "9d231abd-db3d-5d11-9253-820e7eb51742" :question/math-academy-id "q-95712" :question/problem "Find the orthogonal projection matrix that maps $x\\in {R}^{2}$ onto the subspace spanned by an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 18\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nMoreover, ${u}_{i}\\cdot {u}_{i}^{T}$ is the projection matrix corresponding to ${u}_{i}.$\n\nFirst, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to $\\lambda =2.$ Computing $A-2I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-2I & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 18\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 16\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 16\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 16 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=4{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=1,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖v‖=\\sqrt{17}.$ Dividing $v$ by its norm, we obtain the normalized eigenvector: \n\n$$\nu=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, the required orthogonal projection matrix is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {u}^{T} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}16 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cb85388f-97d4-5b7a-9384-bb45d3a9d42b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cb85388f-97d4-5b7a-9384-bb45d3a9d42b" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb85388f-97d4-5b7a-9384-bb45d3a9d42b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e4b2cd88-0c1c-5067-96b8-f34a70eda38d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1d327dec-d42a-581c-8707-926d0b6893a9" "answer-e4b2cd88-0c1c-5067-96b8-f34a70eda38d" "answer-95054c16-a500-55cc-9c6d-5dc257b93966" "answer-3c3ec327-8643-5dfe-8735-8c0774db03ee" "answer-799755e8-7ecf-5b56-8460-da2805b858a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d327dec-d42a-581c-8707-926d0b6893a9" :answer/id #uuid "1d327dec-d42a-581c-8707-926d0b6893a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 16\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4b2cd88-0c1c-5067-96b8-f34a70eda38d" :answer/id #uuid "e4b2cd88-0c1c-5067-96b8-f34a70eda38d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{17}[\\begin{aligned}16 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95054c16-a500-55cc-9c6d-5dc257b93966" :answer/id #uuid "95054c16-a500-55cc-9c6d-5dc257b93966" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 16\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c3ec327-8643-5dfe-8735-8c0774db03ee" :answer/id #uuid "3c3ec327-8643-5dfe-8735-8c0774db03ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}[\\begin{aligned}16 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-799755e8-7ecf-5b56-8460-da2805b858a9" :answer/id #uuid "799755e8-7ecf-5b56-8460-da2805b858a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}[\\begin{aligned}16 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162021 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b502656e-ef35-5f6c-921c-ae3a8ea1f2a2" "question-7e3f233e-913d-50cf-8912-1c6832afca12" "question-69f0b9bd-9336-5c1c-91e3-bf72b33b1333"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b502656e-ef35-5f6c-921c-ae3a8ea1f2a2" :question/id #uuid "b502656e-ef35-5f6c-921c-ae3a8ea1f2a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-95721" :question/problem "Suppose that\n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\n\nare eigenvectors of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ that correspond to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-6,$ respectively. Find the matrix $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nFirst, let's normalize our eigenvectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}{u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}{u}_{2}^{T} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+(-6)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+(-6)\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}((-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+(-6)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}((-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]+(-6)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-25 & 10 \\\\ 10 & -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a49b921e-a620-50dc-993e-f6b1a37ca3f6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a49b921e-a620-50dc-993e-f6b1a37ca3f6" :answer-field/id #uuid "a49b921e-a620-50dc-993e-f6b1a37ca3f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1f090535-e10a-5c59-9a51-2d2aae1cbc9b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1f090535-e10a-5c59-9a51-2d2aae1cbc9b" "answer-5613d7c8-bedb-54d2-be91-7e80b596eb5c" "answer-694df5b3-0ed3-5486-8f0d-63bf6d2b9e75" "answer-3f43beb7-1a8e-5d63-bf78-07894e8c2c04" "answer-bc550768-52c7-5626-83cb-470760bd86c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f090535-e10a-5c59-9a51-2d2aae1cbc9b" :answer/id #uuid "1f090535-e10a-5c59-9a51-2d2aae1cbc9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5613d7c8-bedb-54d2-be91-7e80b596eb5c" :answer/id #uuid "5613d7c8-bedb-54d2-be91-7e80b596eb5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-694df5b3-0ed3-5486-8f0d-63bf6d2b9e75" :answer/id #uuid "694df5b3-0ed3-5486-8f0d-63bf6d2b9e75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f43beb7-1a8e-5d63-bf78-07894e8c2c04" :answer/id #uuid "3f43beb7-1a8e-5d63-bf78-07894e8c2c04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc550768-52c7-5626-83cb-470760bd86c3" :answer/id #uuid "bc550768-52c7-5626-83cb-470760bd86c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7e3f233e-913d-50cf-8912-1c6832afca12" :question/id #uuid "7e3f233e-913d-50cf-8912-1c6832afca12" :question/math-academy-id "q-95725" :question/problem "Suppose that\n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$\n\nare eigenvectors of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ that correspond to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-9,$ respectively. Find the matrix $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nFirst, let's normalize our eigenvectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}{u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}{u}_{2}^{T} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\end{aligned}]+(-9)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\end{aligned}]+(-9)\\cdot \\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}(4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3\\end{aligned}]+(-9)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}(4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}]+(-9)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}[\\begin{aligned}-65 & 78 \\\\ 78 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d1092e23-b9a3-5556-b0d1-0745f95be4b9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d1092e23-b9a3-5556-b0d1-0745f95be4b9" :answer-field/id #uuid "d1092e23-b9a3-5556-b0d1-0745f95be4b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6d264661-257d-5c8a-8684-122b5c0a6807" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d6231cbd-de79-555a-b056-b8008595ed25" "answer-6d264661-257d-5c8a-8684-122b5c0a6807" "answer-9555f6b0-dd96-561e-b956-a28b10613e7e" "answer-16877fa0-d3a3-5da8-ba77-c7e71244a7c0" "answer-ad0b779d-af50-58f8-97aa-dd75027108dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6231cbd-de79-555a-b056-b8008595ed25" :answer/id #uuid "d6231cbd-de79-555a-b056-b8008595ed25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d264661-257d-5c8a-8684-122b5c0a6807" :answer/id #uuid "6d264661-257d-5c8a-8684-122b5c0a6807" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9555f6b0-dd96-561e-b956-a28b10613e7e" :answer/id #uuid "9555f6b0-dd96-561e-b956-a28b10613e7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 6 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16877fa0-d3a3-5da8-ba77-c7e71244a7c0" :answer/id #uuid "16877fa0-d3a3-5da8-ba77-c7e71244a7c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad0b779d-af50-58f8-97aa-dd75027108dd" :answer/id #uuid "ad0b779d-af50-58f8-97aa-dd75027108dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -6 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-69f0b9bd-9336-5c1c-91e3-bf72b33b1333" :question/id #uuid "69f0b9bd-9336-5c1c-91e3-bf72b33b1333" :question/math-academy-id "q-140847" :question/problem "Suppose that\n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\n\nare eigenvectors of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ that correspond to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=8,$ respectively. Find the matrix $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nFirst, let's normalize our eigenvectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}{u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}{u}_{2}^{T} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+8\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+8\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+8\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3b7eee37-4841-5d7e-83f1-ad47a007de82"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3b7eee